From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tomaszstaniak <68373859+tomaszstaniak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 08:59:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] AROS: image logos through datatypes and the Kitty graphics
 subset

Repository: https://github.com/fastfetch-cli/fastfetch
Base: fastfetch 2.70.0, 17bb3fd2384bd814b421d73b8c8b8d08e06cfa26
Problem: the AROS build had no image logos: ENABLE_IMAGE_LOGO needs
ImageMagick or a platform decoder, and upstream's kitty-direct sends a
PNG file name (f=100, t=f), which Limpet does not read. The terminal size
came only from Limpet's presentation reply.
Solution: src/logo/image/image_aros.c implements kitty and kitty-direct.
The picture is decoded by the system's picture datatypes (any format they
read; datatypes.library is opened only then), scaled by area averaging
into whole text cells at the cell size the terminal reports through the
public console geometry packet (ACTION_CONSOLE_GETGEOMETRY), and sent as
RGBA with the Limpet SDK's Kitty encoder. Nothing is sent unless the
terminal confirms the subset in its presentation reply
(XTY_FEATURE_KITTY_GRAPHICS), never in pipe mode; otherwise the small
text logo is shown. Automatic logo detection asks the same capability
instead of a terminal name. The terminal size is taken from the geometry
packet first (Limpet 0.7.0 and any console that takes it up), then from
the presentation reply.
Scope: logo/image/image_aros.c (new), logo/logo.c (AROS: capability test,
small fallback for an image that cannot be shown),
detection/terminalsize/terminalsize_aros.c, CMakeLists.txt (the new file,
FF_HAVE_IMAGE_LOGO for AROS; ENABLE_IMAGE_LOGO stays off).
Upstream-Status: AROS only; part of the AROS backend.
Verification: host test of the scaling (tests/test_port.py); cross-built
for the three targets. Guest runs: docs/evidence/2026-10-27-r2/.
Removal: with the AROS backend.
